From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: REG-Linux <cjom@reglinux.org>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] libretro: don't reassign inputs when no driver is active

retro_load_game_common() returns true on its error path so the core can
draw its own message screen, but it leaves nBurnDrvActive == ~0U. A
frontend that calls retro_set_controller_port_device() after loading
content - RetroArch does, and so does any other frontend following it -
then reaches RefreshControllers() -> GameInpReassign(), which walks the
driver tables through nBurnDrvActive and segfaults.

RetroArch never sees it because it reloads the shared object for every
content load, so bControllersSetOnce is back to false and the refresh is
skipped. A frontend that keeps the core loaded across games hits it as
soon as one game has run: the flag is still set from that game, so the
failed load takes the branch.

Guard the setter on having a driver, and reset the two refresh flags in
InputExit() so unloading really does restore the pre-game state.

--- a/src/burner/libretro/retro_input.cpp
+++ b/src/burner/libretro/retro_input.cpp
@@ -3557,6 +3557,11 @@
 
 	bInputInitialized = false;
 	bLibretroSupportsBitmasks = false;
+	// Put the controller refresh state back the way it is on a fresh
+	// dlopen(), so a frontend which keeps the core loaded between games
+	// starts the next one from the same state as one which reloads it.
+	bControllersNeedRefresh = true;
+	bControllersSetOnce = false;
 }
 
 void retro_set_input_state(retro_input_state_t cb) { input_cb = cb; }
@@ -3606,6 +3611,14 @@
 		}
 	}
 
+	// Without an active driver there is nothing to reassign: the device was
+	// not sanitized above, and RefreshControllers() -> GameInpReassign()
+	// would read the driver tables through nBurnDrvActive == ~0U. That is
+	// reachable because retro_load_game_common() returns true on its error
+	// path so the core can show its own message screen.
+	if (nBurnDrvActive == ~0U)
+		return;
+
 	if (port < nMaxControllers && nDeviceType[port] != device)
 	{
 		nDeviceType[port] = device;
